 "overview": "The Medford Climate Equity Council is a municipal body established to advance local climate resilience, environmental equity, and emissions reduction initiatives. The council reviews city sustainability policies, coordinates public education, and guides community-level climate adaptation and mitigation efforts. Across the 16 meetings recorded between December 2023 and September 2026, the body has tracked home energy coaching, municipal decarbonization projects, composting expansion, flood vulnerability, and public outreach. It also examines infrastructure improvements such as stormwater systems, electric vehicle charging facilities, and public transit accessibility. At its most recent meeting, the council reviewed the city's curbside composting program, discussed hazardous waste protocols, and planned winter heating outreach.",
