  {
   "name": "Curbside composting and solid waste reduction",
   "status": "ongoing",
   "summary": "The city announced a free curbside composting program in early 2024 for residential buildings with four units or fewer. Participation grew rapidly from several hundred residents in the spring to more than five thousand households by late summer, supported by bulk bin distribution events and automatic distribution pilots. The council also explored wider zero-waste initiatives, including swap events and a campaign to phase out non-recyclable black plastic takeout containers. In late 2026, the council reviewed the Garbage to Garden program ahead of municipal trash schedule shifts and discussed proper disposal protocols for lithium-ion batteries and hazardous household waste.",
