  {
   "name": "Stormwater management and flood mitigation",
   "status": "ongoing",
   "summary": "After reviewing flood projection maps through 2070, the council evaluated localized infrastructure needs to manage stormwater and maintain dams. The council voted to approve letters of support for Municipal Vulnerability Preparedness and BRIC grant applications to fund drainage upgrades on Bowen and Golden Avenues as well as Tufts Park. Members subsequently reviewed proposed Green Score zoning mechanisms designed to incentivize stormwater retention and native plantings in FEMA flood zones. In 2026, staff reported that regional grant funding was awarded for a community depaving project but denied for Tufts Park stormwater improvements.",
