  {
   "name": "Municipal building decarbonization and resilience hubs",
   "status": "ongoing",
   "summary": "The council evaluated Medford High School's function as the city's primary emergency shelter and discussed plans for a future multi-service resilience hub. Updates followed regarding a federal earmark request for a resilience hub at the Willis-Appe Community Center, alongside School Committee commitments to HVAC repairs and fossil fuel equipment restrictions. Design work advanced for HVAC electrification at the Andrews and McGlynn schools, though subsequent reports noted delays in high school cooling repairs. The council also monitored long-term planning efforts, including technical assistance for a 30-year municipal building decarbonization roadmap.",
